@startuml system-workflow
title Docling Studio — Workflow (upload a deck, index it, ask RAG, then ask the graph)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C46C

actor "User" as User
participant "Web UI" as UI #E8F5E9
participant "FastAPI\n(app.py)" as API #E3F2FD
participant "converter.py\n+ Docling" as Conv #FFF3E0
participant "Image readers\n(Tesseract · CV)" as Read #F3E5F5
database "Markdown corpus\n(pkg/markdown · knowledge_base)" as Files #ECEFF1
participant "rag.py" as RAG #E8F5E9
participant "md_chunker.py" as Chunk #E3F2FD
boundary "Ollama bge-m3\n(local · :11434)" as Ollama #ECEFF1
database "PostgreSQL\n(pgvector)" as PG #ECEFF1
boundary "Anthropic Claude\n(claude-opus-5)" as Claude #ECEFF1
participant "knowledge_graph.py" as KG #FFF3E0
database "knowledge_graph\n.json" as KGJson #ECEFF1

User -> UI : 1. drops **Workshop.pptx**

== Step 1 — Upload the document ==
UI -> API : POST /api/upload
activate API
API -> Files : save **source.pptx** + name.txt
API -> API : render page previews
API --> UI : doc_id, pages
deactivate API

== Step 2 — Convert it to Markdown ==
UI -> API : POST /api/convert/{doc_id}
activate API
API -> Conv : convert(src)
activate Conv
Conv -> Conv : Docling export_to_markdown()\n+ connector flows → Mermaid
Conv -> Read : embedded pictures
activate Read
Read --> Conv : OCR text · tables · draft flows
deactivate Read
Conv -> Conv : splice into placeholders → **Markdown**
Conv --> API : Result
deactivate Conv
API -> Files : write **output.md**
API --> UI : Markdown + stats
deactivate API

== Step 3 — Chunk, embed and store ==
UI -> API : POST /api/docs/{doc_id}/embed
activate API
API -> Files : copy to knowledge_base/Workshop_pptx.md
API -> RAG : index_file()
activate RAG
RAG -> Files : read .md + SHA-256 fingerprint
Files --> RAG : changed → re-embed
RAG -> Chunk : chunk_file()
Chunk --> RAG : **chunks** (~500 tokens, heading path)
RAG -> Ollama : embed chunks (batches of 32)
Ollama --> RAG : 1024-d **vectors** (never leave the machine)
RAG -> PG : INSERT chunks · vectors · tsvector
deactivate RAG
API --> UI : 42 chunks indexed
deactivate API

== Step 4 — Retrieve the top-k chunks ==
User -> UI : 2. "Who validated 7.1.12.3?"
UI -> API : POST /api/ask (SSE)
activate API
API -> RAG : ask_events(question, k=8)
activate RAG
RAG -> Ollama : embed question
Ollama --> RAG : query vector
RAG -> PG : vector search (cosine, top 40)
PG --> RAG : nearest chunks
RAG -> PG : BM25 keyword search (top 40)
PG --> RAG : keyword matches (codes kept whole)
RAG -> RAG : reciprocal rank fusion → **top 8 excerpts**

== Step 5 — Generate the cited answer ==
RAG -> Claude : excerpts + question (stream)
activate Claude
Claude --> RAG : answer tokens
deactivate Claude
RAG --> API : stage · sources · token events
deactivate RAG
API --> UI : SSE stream
deactivate API
UI --> User : 💬 answer with [n] citations + sources

== Step 6 — Ask the knowledge graph instead ==
User -> UI : 3. "How does eCommerce connect to S/4HANA?"
UI -> API : POST /api/graph/query
activate API
API -> KG : query_graph()
activate KG
KG -> KGJson : load cached graph
KGJson --> KG : 720 nodes · 842 edges
KG -> Files : (on rebuild) re-scan the **same** .md corpus
Files --> KG : streams · systems · BPML codes · SPARK tickets
KG -> KG : resolve entities → BFS shortest path\n+ 2-hop bridge expansion
KG --> API : **templated answer** + node_ids / edge_ids\n(no LLM, no SQL)
deactivate KG
API --> UI : subgraph payload
deactivate API
UI --> User : 🕸️ hop-by-hop path, highlighted on the D3 canvas

note across
  Two engines, one corpus. rag.py embeds with Ollama **on localhost**, runs vector
  AND BM25 search on the same Postgres table, fuses the rankings, and sends Claude
  only the top-k chunks to cite. knowledge_graph.py reads the same .md files with
  regex and answers by **traversing** its graph — no embedding, no database, no LLM.
  The two never call each other.
end note

@enduml
